          <li><strong>20-Day Fast Track:</strong> When applying directly inside Spain via the Ministry of Migration's UGE-CE portal, applications benefit from <em>silencio positivo</em>—if 20 working days pass without a rejection, the permit is granted automatically.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct 3-Year Residency:</strong> In-country applications skip the 1-year paper visa and grant an immediate 3-year biometric foreigner identity card (TIE).</li>
          <li><strong>Clear Route to EU Passport:</strong> Time on the nomad permit counts directly toward the 5-year requirement for EU permanent residency and citizenship.</li>
          <li><a href="/spain-digital-nomad-visa-income-requirements/" class="text-amber-400 underline font-semibold">Read the dedicated Spain DNV statutory guide &rarr;</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Hungary -->
      <section>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-3xl">🇭🇺</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">#3 Hungary (White Card): Low Bureaucratic Friction</h3>
            <span class="text-xs text-blue-400 font-mono">€3,000/mo Threshold • Budget Central European Base</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>
          Hungary's <strong>White Card (Fehér Kártya)</strong> is tailored for individual remote freelancers and tech employees who want low-cost European living without convoluted paperwork:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Consistent €3,000 Threshold:</strong> The National Directorate-General for Aliens Policing (OIF) requires proof of €3,000 per month for the 6 months prior to application.</li>
          <li><strong>Streamlined Approval:</strong> Hungarian consular posts and immigration offices process White Card files within 30 days.</li>
          <li><strong>Individual Constraint:</strong> The White Card strictly does not allow family reunification. Spouses and children cannot be included on the same application.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Portugal -->
      <section>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-3xl">🇵🇹</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">#4 Portugal (D8): The Gold Standard for EU Citizenship</h3>
