          Despite eliminating the original Non-Habitual Resident (NHR) tax holiday, Portugal remains unmatched for remote workers who prioritize obtaining an EU passport:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Statutory Income Formula:</strong> 4 times the Portuguese national minimum monthly remuneration (RMM), totaling <strong>€3,280 per month</strong> in 2026.</li>
          <li><strong>Choice of Two Formats:</strong> A temporary 1-year stay visa (multiple entry) or a 2-year residence permit that transitions into a 3-year extension.</li>
          <li><strong>5-Year Citizenship Guarantee:</strong> Recent amendments to Portugal's Nationality Law allow time to count from the date of initial visa application rather than card issuance, accelerating access to a Tier-1 European passport.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Albania -->
      <section>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-3xl">🇦🇱</span>
